A first-block plus does not take the closer of its div

```
::: d
- d
  - +
:::
after
.
<div class="d">
  <ul>
    <li>d
      <ul>
        <li></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
<p>after</p>
```

```
::: d
:: t
: d
  :: u
  : +
:::
after
.
<div class="d">
  <dl>
    <dt>t</dt>
    <dd>
      <p>d</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>u</dt>
        <dd></dd>
      </dl>
    </dd>
  </dl>
</div>
<p>after</p>
```

```
::: d
- +
:::
after
.
<div class="d">
  <ul>
    <li></li>
  </ul>
</div>
<p>after</p>
```

```
::: d
- d

  > +
:::
after
.
<div class="d">
  <ul>
    <li>d
      <blockquote><p>+</p></blockquote>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
<p>after</p>
```
